{
  "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f9-84a5-fd65e9263256",
  "title": "Executable JARs",
  "sourceUrl": "https://xpandeyed.notion.site/20924eb1ed5480f984a5fd65e9263256",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-0",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot executable archives"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-0-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The Boot build plugin packages application classes and runtime dependencies into an executable JAR."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-0-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A Boot launcher inside the archive loads those classes and dependencies when "
        ],
        [
          "java -jar",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " starts it."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-0-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A servlet application with the standard web starter also includes its embedded Tomcat server."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-0-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The host still needs a compatible Java runtime. The archive does not contain Java itself."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-0-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A database server, credentials, and uploaded application data are separate from the archive."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-1",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Build plugins"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-1-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "spring-boot-maven-plugin",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " repackages Maven\u2019s normal JAR into the Boot executable format."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-1-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The Boot parent supplies the "
        ],
        [
          "repackage",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " execution when that plugin is declared."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-1-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The Boot Gradle plugin provides the equivalent executable JAR task, "
        ],
        [
          "bootJar",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-1-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The build runtime and the deployment runtime must both support the project\u2019s Java version."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-2",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A packaged application"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-2-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Build and run the Maven JAR",
        "language": "text",
        "description": [
          "Java `17` and Maven are required. The files form a separate project rooted at `pom.xml`.",
          "The commands run from the project directory. The second runs after the build succeeds."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "`package` compiles the application and creates `target/demo.jar`.",
          "The plugin repackages that JAR so `java -jar` can load its nested dependencies.",
          "`--server.port=9090` is an application argument read by Boot\u2019s external configuration.",
          "A web application starts its embedded server on port `9090`.",
          "The original non-executable archive may also remain with an `.original` suffix. That file is not the deployable Boot JAR."
        ],
        "commands": "mvn clean package\njava -jar target/demo.jar --server.port=9090",
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/GreetingController.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;\n@RestController\npublic class GreetingController {\n    @GetMapping(\"/\")\n    public String hello() { return \"Hello, Spring Boot\"; }\n}\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-3",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JAR and WAR packaging"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-3-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A traditional WAR deployment also needs servlet-container setup and compatible container versions. Changing the extension is not enough."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-3-table-0",
      "type": "table",
      "columnOrder": [
        "0",
        "1"
      ],
      "hasColumnHeader": true,
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-3-table-0-row-0",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "Archive"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "Typical deployment"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-3-table-0-row-1",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "Executable Boot JAR"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "A Java process with its embedded server."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-3-table-0-row-2",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "WAR"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "An application deployed to a separately managed servlet container."
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-4",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Runtime configuration"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-4-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The same JAR can use different profiles and external properties on different hosts."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-4-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Credentials belong in the host\u2019s secret or configuration system, rather than in the packaged source files."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-4-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A successful build proves packaging completed. Startup logs and application requests check the running release."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "executable-jars-deployment-lesson-4-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The next lessons cover the Boot settings needed for managed hosting, a VPS process, and an HTTPS proxy."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
